Changed: SparseDirectMUMPS::get_icntl() now returns a pointer to
types::mumps_index instead of int, matching the integer type of the MUMPS
installation. Code that explicitly stores the returned pointer as int * must
use types::mumps_index * or auto * to also support 64-bit MUMPS integers.
<br>
(Luca Heltai, 2026/10/18)
